LIMIT;
+++++++
 LIMIT defines how many rows should be returned from the result set.


i want first 2 row:
------------------
SELECT *
FROM EMP
LIMIT 2 ;

OFFSET:
++++++

FFSET defines how many rows should be skipped before returning results.

SELECT *
FROM EMP
LIMIT 2 OFFSET 2;

i want 3rd and 4th row.
------------------------
 Skip first 2 rows (OFFSET 2)
 Return next 2 rows (LIMIT 2)

i want 7th row.
----------------------
SELECT *
FROM EMP
LIMIT 1 OFFSET 6;




TO FIND MAX SALERY BY USING OFFSET AND LIMIT:(DESC)
----------------------------------------------

2ND MAX SAL:

SELECT DISTINCT SAL
FROM EMP
ORDER BY SAL DESC
LIMIT 1 OFFSET 2;

5TH MAX SAL:

SELECT DISTINCT SAL
FROM EMP
ORDER BY SAL DESC
LIMIT 1 OFFSET 4;




TO FIND MIN SALERY BY USING OFFSET AND LIMIT:(ACS)
---------------------------------------------


3RD MIN :

SELECT DISTINCT SAL
FROM EMP
ORDER BY SAL ASC
LIMIT 1 OFFSET 2;
